<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14962" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dū^pondĭārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		dupondius, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>containing two</i> asses. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orbiculus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					4, 30, 4</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dŭpondĭ-ārĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m. (sc. nummus), <i>a
				two-as piece</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 34, 2, 2, §
			4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, like diobolaris, <i>worth two coppers</i>, i. e. <i>worthless</i>,
				<i>bad</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dominus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 58, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 74, 15</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
